{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790261834036,"sessionID":"ses_f2c171405ffevkjU3ihajBZgBm","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_cca1af6748eb46ab865c731a","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Explore project structure","prompt":"Explore the /workspace directory thoroughly. I need to understand:\n1. The full directory structure (all files and folders)\n2. Any existing .tscn, .gd, .gdshader files\n3. The contents of any existing scripts, scenes, or shaders\n4. Any project.godot or similar configuration files\n5. Any spritesheet textures (look for .png files)\n6. Any existing towerDefense-related assets\n\nReturn the complete directory tree and the contents of all relevant files.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"<task id=\"ses_f2c16be76ffer0Pi48NSaBjekn\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nHere is a comprehensive report of everything found in `/workspace`.\n\n---\n\n## Complete Directory Tree\n\n```\n/workspace/\n├── .godot/                                    # Godot editor metadata & cache (auto-generated)\n│   ├── .gdignore                              # Empty file, tells Godot to ignore this directory for imports\n│   ├── uid_cache.bin                          # Binary UID cache\n│   ├── scene_groups_cache.cfg                 # Groups cache (maps player.tscn -> \"units\" group)\n│   ├── global_script_class_cache.cfg          # Empty script class cache\n│   ├── editor/\n│   │   ├── filesystem_cache10                 # Filesystem cache (timestamps, types, dependencies)\n│   │   ├── main.tscn-folding-*.cfg            # Editor folding state for main.tscn\n│   │   └── project_metadata.cfg               # Editor metadata (Godot binary path: /run/gamedevbench-bin/godot)\n│   └── imported/\n│       ├── towerDefense_tilesheet.png-*.ctex  # Compressed texture (binary cache)\n│       └── towerDefense_tilesheet.png-*.md5   # MD5 cache (source: ed9b168a..., dest: 98ef458b...)\n│\n├── assets/\n│   ├── shaders/\n│   │   ├── aura.gdshader                       # Canvas-item shader for selection aura highlight\n│   │   └── aura.gdshader.uid                   # UID: uid://c1ejn7kg46g2\n│   └── sprites/\n│       ├── towerDefense_tilesheet.png           # Spritesheet texture (PNG image)\n│       └── towerDefense_tilesheet.png.import    # Import settings (CompressedTexture2D)\n│\n├── scenes/\n│   ├── main.tscn                               # Main scene (Node2D root, 2x Unit instances)\n│   └── player.tscn                             # Reusable Unit scene (CharacterBody2D, groups=[\"units\"])\n│\n├── scripts/\n│   ├── unit.gd                                 # Unit script (CharacterBody2D, mostly stubbed out)\n│   └── unit.gd.uid                             # UID: uid://crm11wc00tqd4\n│\n├── project.godot                               # Godot project config (GL Compatibility, Godot 4.4)\n└── task_config.json                            # Task instruction JSON\n```\n\n---\n\n## File Contents\n\n### 1. `/workspace/project.godot` (Project Configuration)\n```ini\nconfig_version=5\n\n[application]\nconfig/name=\"Configure RTS Unit Scene with Aura Highlight\"\nconfig/description=\"A simple task to test CUA ability to move a player asset to the origin coordinates\"\nrun/main_scene=\"res://scenes/main.tscn\"\nconfig/features=PackedStringArray(\"4.4\")\n\n[rendering]\nrenderer/rendering_method=\"gl_compatibility\"\n```\n- **Godot 4.4**, GL Compatibility renderer. Main scene is `main.tscn`.\n\n---\n\n### 2. `/workspace/task_config.json` (Task Instructions)\n```json\n{\n  \"instruction\": \"Build the reusable Unit scene: root it in a CharacterBody2D on collision layer 2/mask 3, keep it in the 'units' group. Add a Sprite2D child that uses the towerDefense spritesheet texture with region_enabled=true and region_rect=Rect2(960, 640, 64, 64), and apply a ShaderMaterial using the aura.gdshader. Add a CollisionShape2D child with a CircleShape2D of radius 14. Add an Area2D child named 'Detect' (collision layer 2, collision mask 2) with its own CollisionShape2D child using a CircleShape2D of radius 35. Implement unit.gd to export a speed variable, define a target_radius variable, include set_selected() and set_target() setters, an avoid() function that uses $Detect.get_overlapping_bodies(), and use move_and_collide() for movement. The set_selected() function must toggle the aura_width shader parameter (1.0 when selected=true, 0.0 when selected=false). Duplicate the Sprite2D material in _ready() to ensure each instance has its own material.\"\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. `/workspace/scenes/main.tscn` (Main Scene)\n```ini\n[gd_scene load_steps=2 format=3]\n\n[ext_resource type=\"PackedScene\" path=\"res://scenes/player.tscn\" id=\"1_lv2sa\"]\n\n[node name=\"Main\" type=\"Node2D\"]\n\n[node name=\"UnitA\" parent=\".\" instance=ExtResource(\"1_lv2sa\")]\nposition = Vector2(180, 160)\n\n[node name=\"UnitB\" parent=\".\" instance=ExtResource(\"1_lv2sa\")]\nposition = Vector2(360, 200)\n```\n- Root node: `Node2D` named \"Main\"\n- Two instances of `player.tscn`: **UnitA** at (180, 160) and **UnitB** at (360, 200)\n\n---\n\n### 4. `/workspace/scenes/player.tscn` (Reusable Unit Scene)\n```ini\n[gd_scene load_steps=2 format=3]\n\n[ext_resource type=\"Script\" path=\"res://scripts/unit.gd\" id=\"1_vv7m8\"]\n\n[node name=\"Unit\" type=\"CharacterBody2D\" groups=[\"units\"]]\nscript = ExtResource(\"1_vv7m8\")\n```\n- Root: `CharacterBody2D` named \"Unit\", belongs to the **\"units\"** group, attached to `unit.gd`.\n- Currently **missing** all required children (Sprite2D, CollisionShape2D, Area2D/Detect).\n\n---\n\n### 5. `/workspace/scripts/unit.gd` (Unit Script -- STUBBED)\n```gd\nextends CharacterBody2D\n\n# Implement movement, selection highlight, and avoidance logic in this script.\n# The test expects exported speed/target settings, setter methods that toggle the\n# aura shader, and an avoid() helper that inspects the Detect Area2D.\n```\n- Only a comment block. The actual logic (exported `speed`, `target_radius`, `set_selected()`, `set_target()`, `avoid()`, `_ready()` shader material duplication) is not yet implemented.\n\n---\n\n### 6. `/workspace/assets/shaders/aura.gdshader` (Aura Shader)\n```gdshader\nshader_type canvas_item;\n//render_mode blend_premul_alpha;\n\nuniform float aura_width = 2.0;\nuniform vec4 aura_color : source_color;\n\nvoid fragment() {\n\tvec4 col = texture(TEXTURE, UV);\n\tvec2 ps = TEXTURE_PIXEL_SIZE;\n\tfloat a;\n\tfloat maxa = col.a;\n\tfloat mina = col.a;\n\n\ta = texture(TEXTURE, UV + vec2(0.0, -aura_width) * ps).a;\n\tmaxa = max(a, maxa);\n\tmina = min(a, mina);\n\n\ta = texture(TEXTURE, UV + vec2(0.0, aura_width) * ps).a;\n\tmaxa = max(a, maxa);\n\tmina = min(a, mina);\n\n\ta = texture(TEXTURE, UV + vec2(-aura_width, 0.0) * ps).a;\n\tmaxa = max(a, maxa);\n\tmina = min(a, mina);\n\n\ta = texture(TEXTURE, UV + vec2(aura_width, 0.0) * ps).a;\n\tmaxa = max(a, maxa);\n\tmina = min(a, mina);\n\n\tcol.rgb *= col.a;\n\n\tCOLOR = col;\n\tCOLOR.rgb += aura_color.rgb * (maxa - mina);\n}\n```\n- A 2D edge-detection / outline shader. Samples neighboring pixels at `aura_width` distance, adds `aura_color` to pixels at the boundary of opaque regions. The `aura_width` uniform (default 2.0) controls outline thickness.\n\n---\n\n### 7. `/workspace/assets/sprites/towerDefense_tilesheet.png` (Spritesheet Texture)\n- A PNG spritesheet image, imported as `CompressedTexture2D` (compressed .ctex in `.godot/imported/`).\n- According to `task_config.json`, the target tile is at region `Rect2(960, 640, 64, 64)`.\n- Source MD5: `ed9b168ac272e560c9fe2563f60c46a2`\n\n---\n\n### 8. `/workspace/assets/sprites/towerDefense_tilesheet.png.import` (Import Settings)\n```ini\n[remap]\nimporter=\"texture\"\ntype=\"CompressedTexture2D\"\nuid=\"uid://171p6dp3lfto\"\n\n[params]\ncompress/mode=0\nmipmaps/generate=false\nprocess/fix_alpha_border=true\ndetect_3d/compress_to=1\n```\n\n---\n\n## Summary of Tower-Defense-Related Assets\n\n| Asset | Path | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Spritesheet** | `/workspace/assets/sprites/towerDefense_tilesheet.png` | Tower-defense tile spritesheet (PNG) |\n| **Aura Shader** | `/workspace/assets/shaders/aura.gdshader` | Canvas-item outline/aura shader for unit selection highlight |\n| **Unit Scene** | `/workspace/scenes/player.tscn` | Reusable CharacterBody2D scene (in \"units\" group) -- needs children added per task_config.json |\n| **Main Scene** | `/workspace/scenes/main.tscn` | Node2D with two Unit instances (UnitA, UnitB) |\n| **Unit Script** | `/workspace/scripts/unit.gd` | Stubbed script -- needs full implementation per task_config.json |\n| **Task Config** | `/workspace/task_config.json` | Detailed build instructions for the RTS unit with aura highlight |\n\n---\n\n## Key Observations\n\n1. **The project is a Godot 4.4 project** using the GL Compatibility renderer.\n2. **The player.tscn scene is incomplete** -- it only has a CharacterBody2D root with the unit.gd script attached. It is missing the required Sprite2D, CollisionShape2D, and Area2D/Detect children.\n3. **The unit.gd script is a stub** -- only comments, no actual implementation.\n4. **The main.tscn scene** already instantiates two copies of `player.tscn` at different positions, which means once `player.tscn` is completed, both units will be fully functional.\n5. **The aura.gdshader** is complete and ready to use for the selection highlight effect.\n6. **The spritesheet** is present and imported. The specific tile to use is at pixel region (960, 640, 64, 64).\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_f2c171405ffevkjU3ihajBZgBm","sessionId":"ses_f2c16be76ffer0Pi48NSaBjekn","model":{"modelID":"deepseek-v4-pro","providerID":"openai"},"truncated":false},"title":"Explore project structure","time":{"start":1790261674381,"end":1790261834026}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_c228a6b5-114e-4b63-85ac-5f8bfe6b3f4c"}},"id":"prt_0d3e9417d0011kYd82Xt9ooIB9","sessionID":"ses_f2c171405ffevkjU3ihajBZgBm","messageID":"msg_0d3e8e